# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Kairo API server — environment variables
# Copy to .env.local for local dev; set the same names on the Vercel project
# "kairo-api" (Production) for the deployed backend.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── REQUIRED: credential persistence ─────────────────────────────────────────
# PostgreSQL connection string. MUST be IPv4-reachable: Vercel serverless
# functions cannot dial IPv6, and Supabase DIRECT hosts (db.<ref>.supabase.co)
# are IPv6-only (verified via DNS: zero A records). Use the Session Pooler
# host instead — Supabase dashboard → Connect → Session pooler.
#
# Format (note the username is "postgres.<project-ref>", NOT plain "postgres"):
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.wjuuxkgvggmuhecnwmzg:<YOUR-PASSWORD>@aws-0-<REGION>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres"
#
# The pooler host has IPv4 A records (verified: aws-0-us-east-1.pooler.supabase.com
# → 44.216.29.125 etc.). Percent-encode special characters in the password.
# If DATABASE_URL is unset, credentials are session-only (process memory).

# ── REQUIRED with DATABASE_URL: encryption at rest ───────────────────────────
# 32 bytes as 64 hex chars (or base64). Generate: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# Set once and NEVER change it afterwards — rotating it makes every stored
# credential row undecryptable ("unreadable" state in the UI).
# A valid 32-byte key is ALREADY SET on the kairo-api Vercel project (Session 10).
CREDENTIALS_ENCRYPTION_KEY=""

# ── Auth (Clerk) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=""
# Not currently read by API code, but already present on Vercel:
CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=""

# ── AI chat (PowerX) — server-side only, never exposed to the browser ────────
# Bearer token for the PowerX gateway. The current px_… token was issued by
# the retired Render deployment and is rejected by the code.run gateway
# ("Invalid API key") — obtain a fresh token from the PowerX owner.
POWERX_API_TOKEN=""
# Overrides (defaults shown):
# POWERX_API_URL="https://http--powerx-app--cmttpj77q5vc.code.run/v1"
# POWERX_MODEL="powerx-agent"
# POWERX_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS="15000"
# POWERX_POLL_INTERVAL_MS="2000"
# POWERX_POLL_TIMEOUT_MS="30000"

# ── CORS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated frontend origin allowlist.
CORS_ORIGINS=""

# ── Optional: fallback Alpaca keys (per-user keys from the UI take priority) ─
# ALPACA_API_KEY=""
# ALPACA_API_SECRET=""

# ── Local dev only — MUST NEVER be set in production ─────────────────────────
# Bypasses Clerk auth; every request becomes user "local-dev-user".
# ALLOW_LOCAL_DEV_AUTH="true"
